# Project Rule Index

This file defines global priorities. Detailed guidance is split into focused rules:

- `architecture-nextjs.mdc`
- `components-and-styling.mdc`
- `collaboration-preferences.mdc`
- `content-and-data.mdc`
- `figma-to-code-delivery.mdc`
- `homepage-delivery-and-responsive.mdc`
- `quality-gates.mdc`
- `security-and-runtime.mdc`
- `shadcn-ui-components.mdc`

## Global Priorities (always apply)

- Prefer existing project patterns over inventing new architecture.
- Keep changes minimal, readable, and consistent with neighboring files.
- Default to Server Components and small Client Component islands.
- Reuse shared UI (`Section`, `Button`, `Breadcrumb`, cards, grids) before creating new variants.
- Keep long marketing copy in `data/` unless it is tiny one-off text.
- Build layouts mobile-first, then extend to larger breakpoints.
- Follow the Figma-to-code section workflow before implementing new UI.
- Maintain Czech-first content style unless the task explicitly requires another locale.

## Done Criteria

- Updated code matches route/component/data structure already used in this repo.
- New pages/components pass lint and basic accessibility checks.
- Homepage changes are verified at mobile and desktop breakpoints without overflow.
- Figma-driven sections are mapped to reusable components and data before polish.
- New routes include metadata considerations and correct image/link semantics.